From: Pyra kernel work <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] arm: dts: lc15: restore the AESS audio routes

omap5-board-common.dtsi routes the codec's downlink stream widgets to the
AESS back ends:

	"Headset Playback", "PDM_DL1",
	"Handsfree Playback", "PDM_DL2",

omap5-letux-cortex15-common.dtsi overrides ti,audio-routing wholesale and does
not carry them. That was harmless for as long as the AESS was dead. With 0019
putting the AESS graph in place it is the last missing link: the path runs
MM1 Playback -> MM VMixer -> MM_DL -> DL1 Mixer -> Sidetone Mixer -> DL1 PDM
-> PDM_DL1 and then stops, because nothing joins PDM_DL1 to the codec.

"Headset Playback" and "Handsfree Playback" are the stream names of the
twl6040's twl6040-dl1 and twl6040-dl2 DAIs, so these two routes connect the
graph recovered from the AESS firmware to the codec the board actually has.

The board's other dropped routes are not restored here. "PDM_UL1", "Analog
Capture" names a widget this codec does not have -- twl6040-ul's stream is
"Capture" -- and the McBSP routes belong to the bluetooth and FM cards, which
have their own simple-card links on this board. Only the two that playback
needs are added, and only those are verified.

The DTB builds.

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/omap5-letux-cortex15-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/omap5-letux-cortex15-common.dtsi
@@ -432,7 +432,22 @@
 		"HSMIC", "Headset Mic",
 		"Headset Mic", "Headset Mic Bias",
 		"MAINMIC", "Main Handset Mic",
-		"Main Handset Mic", "Main Mic Bias";
+		"Main Handset Mic", "Main Mic Bias",
+
+		/*
+		 * The AESS back ends. omap5-board-common.dtsi has these and
+		 * this override dropped them, which was harmless while the
+		 * AESS was dead: with it running they are the last link in
+		 * the chain, joining the codec's DL1 and DL2 stream widgets
+		 * to the AESS graph, and without them the path ends at
+		 * PDM_DL1 and never reaches the twl6040.
+		 *
+		 * "Headset Playback" and "Handsfree Playback" are the stream
+		 * names of the codec's twl6040-dl1 and twl6040-dl2 DAIs; the
+		 * AESS side comes from its firmware's own widget list.
+		 */
+		"Headset Playback", "PDM_DL1",
+		"Handsfree Playback", "PDM_DL2";
 };
 
 &twl6040_pins {
